<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Alwali II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1781">1781</a>–<a href="/years/1807">1807</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad Alwali</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Alwali II was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a>, ruling from 1781. When the Fulani jihad of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a> spread in the early 1800s, he fought the local jihadist leaders but was defeated and driven from Kano by 1807, and he was killed soon afterwards. Kano then became an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
